78	    // VS at Off (e.g. an OS context-switched the regs away before the
79	    // trigger fired) -- gating the write on the drained field skips the
80	    // enable and silently NACKs every subsequent FPR / V-CSR write. Always
81	    // write mstatus when either extension is in scope; force-OR Initial
82	    // when the drained field is Off. This enable is local to the vsim
83	    // phase; the state.mstatus written to the handoff file is left
